<urn:beads-cache:finding:RSH-001> triage:startupReopenEvidence "{\"finding\": {\"category\": \"correctness\", \"evidence\": \"Independent source-free public-API probe at45c9dd1 retains Composed::schedule_store(), starts its ordinary set_enabled write under a real external BEGIN IMMEDIATE writer and proves actual same-connection mutex contention via a bounded worker view notification. Then Application::start(grace250ms) and actual shutdown remain pending902.343541ms (>original2T500ms); after explicit writer ROLLBACK, management returnsOk(true), both probe/management threads join and Application returnsOk at978.142166ms. Direct probe process exited0 and was waited/reaped; no product edits/private access. Source cron171 warn_at_startup()->schedule.rows760 reads original management store before stop loop and deadlines200+.\", \"file\": \"crates/bd-cache-sync/src/cron.rs\", \"id\": \"RSH-001\", \"issue\": \"The qualified post-start worker/store correction is consumed correctly, but the public startup path still reads warnings through the unbounded management view before observing stop. A supported retained schedule view can hold that shared connection during an ordinary management write, extending an actual Application shutdown beyond2T before the bounded worker starts.\", \"line\": 171, \"owning_sprint\": \"c-1\", \"probe_receipt\": \"/tmp/phase-c-execution/c-2/qa-5/startup-probe-result.json\", \"recommendation\": \"Route this newly discovered startup occurrence to the C1 shared cron producer owner: make startup work stop-aware and cooperatively bounded within the existing absolute2T lifetime, preserving real owned joins and ordinary independent management policy. Add a deterministic early-stop/shared-connection regression. No new SDK surface, detached task, timeout widening or management-policy suppression is required by this finding. After the producer correction, consume the exact source and requalify the caller.\", \"reviewer\": \"rust-qa-agent\", \"scope_limit\": \"This is the generic public cron/start-stop contract and a real public Application API reproduction. Current stock daemon composition itself does not launch this independent pre-start same-connection management writer; no stock-daemon HTTP reproduction is asserted. Genuine post-start worker/store/reader caller qualification remains credited.\", \"severity\": \"critical\"}, \"owner_task\": \"/root/c2_rustqa4\", \"probe\": \"/tmp/phase-c-execution/c-2/qa-5/startup-probe-result.json\", \"qualified_shared_producer\": \"5255610a16ef4500f0af508e29a533707a4a3e0a\", \"scope\": \"New supported public Application/SystemSchedules startup occurrence owned by C1 cron prelude, no documented startup exclusion; stock daemon HTTP reproduction not claimed. Prior post-start fixes remain credited.\", \"source_commit\": \"45c9dd13258482ba8af3e5cfeae5ce146b120453\", \"status\": \"open\"}" .

<urn:beads-cache:finding:RSH-001> triage:startupCandidateProducerHistory "{\"context\": \"Immutable C1 candidate history retained on merge; owning C2 status and earlier history above stay authoritative. C1 QA8 remains FAIL; no acceptance inferred.\", \"producer_ttl\": \"@prefix triage: <urn:beads-cache:triage:> .\\n<urn:beads-cache:finding:RSH-001> triage:id \\\"RSH-001\\\" ; triage:sprint \\\"c-1\\\" ; triage:severity \\\"critical\\\" ; triage:location \\\"crates/bd-cache-sync/src/cron.rs:198\\\" ; triage:source \\\"qa-3 owning reviewer fenced JSON\\\" ; triage:status \\\"open\\\" ; triage:record \\\"{\\\\\\\"carry_forward_from\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"qa-2 specialist output; unchanged production source, still open\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"OPEN at assigned HEAD: crates/bd-cache-sync/src/cron.rs:198 still constructs worker.shutdown(now + shutdown_timeout), :202 awaits it, :214 awaits that same future after a hurried stop, and :217-225 calls the ordinary expiry kill/callback only after shutdown returns. Cargo.toml:36 and Cargo.lock:1153-1154 remain published sc-cron exactly 0.1.1. Its actual installed registry source /Users/randlee/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/sc-cron-0.1.1/src/scheduler.rs:912-931 still times out then awaits task without abort; worker.rs:539-550 still awaits an uncancelled blocking store call. Thus the original contended reload/persistence occurrence remains. No workaround or baseline change was introduced. The sprint explicitly records this blocker at docs/plans/phase-c/sprint-c-1-runtime-migration.md:511 and :540-545.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"crates/bd-cache-sync/src/cron.rs\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"RSH-001\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"issue\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The migrated shutdown call no longer enforces the existing bounded stop contract. Published sc-cron 0.1.1 waits for its worker even after the handle deadline. A worker awaiting a contended shared-store call can therefore keep cron_run_hurried beyond T and its documented 2*T total bound; on the ordinary expiry path the bd-kill callback is itself delayed until that wait ends. A second signal also awaits the same unresolved shutdown future at line 211. This violates REQ-BDC-0730 and the preserved REQ-CRON-0012 semantics.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"line\\\\\\\": 198, \\\\\\\"recommendation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Resolve the mismatch upstream and qualify an approved bounded-shutdown contract before accepting the migration. Ensure expiry triggers kill immediately and cleanup finishes within the existing absolute shutdown bound, including a worker blocked in reload/persistence. Do not fork the scheduler or replace the bound with an async timeout that leaves detached ownership behind.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reviewer\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rust-service-hardening-agent\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"critical\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"topic\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"graceful_shutdown\\\\\\\"}\\\" .\\n\\n<urn:beads-cache:finding:RSH-001> triage:restartEvidence \\\"{\\\\\\\"branch\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"sprint/c-1-runtime-migration\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"docs/plans/phase-c/sprint-c-1-runtime-migration.md#consumer-restart-correction-bounded-cache-scheduler-shutdown\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"RSH-001\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"implementation_state\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"implemented_pending_independent_QA\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"logs\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"/tmp/phase-c-execution/c-1/qa-4/restart-*.log\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"source\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"C1 restart developer assessment; independent QA pending\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"open\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"summary\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Cache-owned dynamic store cancellation and same-Scheduler management isolation; real worker join, original 2*T deadline, expiry/second-stop callback, zero timeout and reuse regressions.\\\\\\\"}\\\" .\\n\\n<urn:beads-cache:finding:RSH-001> triage:closureEvidence \\\"{\\\\\\\"enforcer_task\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"/root/c1_quality_manager4\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"/tmp/phase-c-execution/c-1/qa-4/rust-service-hardening-agent-result.json\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"owner_task\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"/root/c1_service4\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"pr_comment_url\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"https://github.com/randlee/beads-cache/pull/108#issuecomment-6620322598\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"qa_pass\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"qa-4\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reviewed_commit\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"95def5f3c1c2ffe7a0e9ebfe3630ac835217c680\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"scope\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Production boundedshutdownfinding only; FTQ009/010separateopen Importanttestcleanupfindings; no wholeC1acceptance.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"closed\\\\\\\"}\\\" .\\n\\n<urn:beads-cache:finding:RSH-001> triage:startupReopenEvidence \\\"{\\\\\\\"finding\\\\\\\": {\\\\\\\"category\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"correctness\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"evidence\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Independent source-free public-API probe at45c9dd1 retains Composed::schedule_store(), starts its ordinary set_enabled write under a real external BEGIN IMMEDIATE writer and proves actual same-connection mutex contention via a bounded worker view notification. Then Application::start(grace250ms) and actual shutdown remain pending902.343541ms (>original2T500ms); after explicit writer ROLLBACK, management returnsOk(true), both probe/management threads join and Application returnsOk at978.142166ms. Direct probe process exited0 and was waited/reaped; no product edits/private access. Source cron171 warn_at_startup()->schedule.rows760 reads original management store before stop loop and deadlines200+.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"file\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"crates/bd-cache-sync/src/cron.rs\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"RSH-001\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"issue\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"The qualified post-start worker/store correction is consumed correctly, but the public startup path still reads warnings through the unbounded management view before observing stop. A supported retained schedule view can hold that shared connection during an ordinary management write, extending an actual Application shutdown beyond2T before the bounded worker starts.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"line\\\\\\\": 171, \\\\\\\"owning_sprint\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"c-1\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"probe_receipt\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"/tmp/phase-c-execution/c-2/qa-5/startup-probe-result.json\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"recommendation\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"Route this newly discovered startup occurrence to the C1 shared cron producer owner: make startup work stop-aware and cooperatively bounded within the existing absolute2T lifetime, preserving real owned joins and ordinary independent management policy. Add a deterministic early-stop/shared-connection regression. No new SDK surface, detached task, timeout widening or management-policy suppression is required by this finding. After the producer correction, consume the exact source and requalify the caller.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"reviewer\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"rust-qa-agent\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"scope_limit\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"This is the generic public cron/start-stop contract and a real public Application API reproduction. Current stock daemon composition itself does not launch this independent pre-start same-connection management writer; no stock-daemon HTTP reproduction is asserted. Genuine post-start worker/store/reader caller qualification remains credited.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"severity\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"critical\\\\\\\"}, \\\\\\\"owner_task\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"/root/c2_rustqa4\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"probe\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"/tmp/phase-c-execution/c-2/qa-5/startup-probe-result.json\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"qualified_shared_producer\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"5255610a16ef4500f0af508e29a533707a4a3e0a\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"scope\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"New supported public Application/SystemSchedules startup occurrence owned by C1 cron prelude, no documented startup exclusion; stock daemon HTTP reproduction not claimed. Prior post-start fixes remain credited.\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"source_commit\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"45c9dd13258482ba8af3e5cfeae5ce146b120453\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\": \\\\\\\"open\\\\\\\"}\\\" .\\n\\n<urn:beads-cache:finding:RSH-001> triage:startupCorrection \\